  "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
  "instance_name": "performative_emotion_stereotype",
  "label": "Stereotype of exaggerated emotional reactions in public settings",
  "description": "The image of the man with an exaggerated expression of shock or excitement is culturally coded as a 'performative' or 'over-the-top' emotional reaction, often seen in sports, entertainment, or other public events. This stereotype is used to create humor or irony by implying the person is reacting in an absurdly dramatic way. The meme relies on this stereotype to contrast with the sentiment of maternal love, suggesting that the emotion being displayed is somehow 'unworthy' or 'exaggerated' compared to the supposed depth of maternal love. This requires background knowledge of how public emotional displays are perceived and mocked in popular culture.",
